":"BUTTERFLY/v1\n\nsymptom: `FRIDAY-RELEASE-COMMANDER-0001` received a multi-hour P(-1) authority mandate but the mailbox executed it as a one-shot task: CLAIMED -> EXECUTION_FINISHED(exit=0) in ~50s -> TASK_BLOCKED with `artifact_count: 0`.\nintegration_context: This appeared only when a long-lived release authority was expressed through the existing task mailbox. The executor/reporting pipeline correctly knows how to terminate a task, but has no durable semantic distinction between completion of one invocation and expiry/completion of an authority role.\ncocoon: Missing primitive `RoleLease` / `CommanderLease`, distinct from `TaskLease`. A role lease must survive subordinate process termination and remain active until `deadline | revoke | budget_exhausted | sovereign_boundary`, while each subordinate task retains ordinary strict settlement.\npossible_feature: deadline-bound persistent commander control loop: RECONCILE -> choose blockage -> delegate/execute -> inspect evidence -> replan -> continue. Commander must not become completion oracle; strict task reporter remains authoritative for subordinate work.\ncheapest_falsification: run a bounded synthetic commander lease with two subordinate no-op/evidence tasks. Prove task A can terminate/settle while commander remains ACTIVE and launches task B; then prove commander stops exactly on explicit expiry/revoke without replaying either subordinate semantic effect.\ndecision: adopt_now as design finding; do not redesign mailbox during the current release window unless the directly bootstrapped commander itself chooses the minimal implementation as necessary for Friday evidence.\n\nPrometheus note: current #121 is a canonical `END=yes / DONE=no` fixture. Do not blindly rerun this same mailbox task. A direct sovereign bootstrap outside the one-shot mailbox has been provided by Pasha for today's experiment.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cy